From 5fd70ea6573b733df79cb0ee300b1a63a7357e44 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yangsonglin13 <yangsonglin566@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 19:27:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] fix(rfork): harden weight reuse and planner recovery

Include effective P/D model and layout switches in stable compatibility fingerprints while excluding runtime-only settings. Surface successful TP0 raw weight-read timing at INFO and keep other transfer detail at DEBUG.

Keep healthy seed services available after transient planner advertisement failures, retry registration and lease release in the background, and limit outage logs to first failure, periodic summaries, and recovery. Permanent planner rejections still prevent seed promotion.

Reject reads when the destination registration cache is missing instead of rescanning potentially unregistered buffers. Remove the redundant local-only excluded-block check while preserving seed-shared reconciliation. Update documentation and regression tests.

Signed-off-by: yangsonglin13 <yangsonglin566@gmail.com>
